  "articleBody": "Choosing the right garage floor can feel a bit overwhelming with all the options out there. To simplify it, you'll want to think about what really matters to you. First, consider the installer's experience. Are they certified or trained in the specific system you're interested in? That's a huge plus. Always ask about their insurance too; you want peace of mind. Product quality is key – cheaper isn't always better here. Look for a manufacturer-backed warranty, as that shows they stand behind their materials. And don't shy away from asking for a clear explanation of their surface preparation methods and what's included in the price. Things like moisture testing and proper concrete profiling are non-negotiable for a durable floor. If your garage slab has existing issues like cracks, old coatings, or drains, a qualified professional can help you navigate those complexities and choose a system that will actually last. Don't hesitate to reach out to HH Remodeling LLC in the greater Denver area for guidance; we're happy to walk you through the options.",
